an, like we did earlier... Instead, you did it for a cube.\" I need to apologize immediately, because I look stupid. I completely misunderstood their instructions, and I'll explain my error in the next message.\n\n\n**Apologizing & Clarifying Story**\n\nI'm apologizing for the earlier misinterpretation; my cube-based \"story\" approach was lazy. I should have gone for the 3D stickman from the start. I'm now drafting the script to create a true 3D stickman, and I will be able to render a 5-second walk cycle. I am trying to build a true 3D stickman.\n\n\n**Building The Rig**\n\nI'm now focused on constructing the rig for the 3D stickman's body. I'm using Empties as pivot points for each joint, employing a straightforward forward kinematics approach. I'm adding a white material to the cylinders. I'll parent the cylinders to the Empties to get a walking motion. Specifically, I'm constructing body, head, shoulder, arm, and leg parts, and I'll parent them to each other.\n\n\n**Constructing The Animation**\n\nI'm now building the 3D stickman and focusing on adding the animation with the script. It's becoming straightforward forward kinematics. I'm adding spheres and cylinders for the parts of the 3D stickman's body: head, body, shoulders, arms, legs and I will set joints. I will implement a five-second walk cycle. I'm excited with how it looks so far.\n\n\n**Finalizing The Scene**\n\nI'm now completing the 3D stickman scene. I'm adding spheres and cylinders for the body, joints for rotation, and placing them with the proper offset. I've added a ground plane and a camera, setting their materials, position, and rotation, and added a light for a nice render. I'm getting close to running the animation script!\n\n\n**Animating The Stickman**\n\nI'm now implementing the walk cycle using Blender's Python API, including animations for body bounce and leg movement. I've set the scene's frame rate and length to 30fps and 5 seconds, respectively, which is 150 frames. Keyframes are being inserted for body location, hip rotation and knee rotation, which will provide the walking motion. The parameters provide a decent 3D stickman animation.\n\n\n**Coding Walk Cycle**\n\nI'm now integrating the arm and head bob animations into my Python script. I'm adding `math.sin` functions to generate the keyframes for shoulder, elbow, and head rotations to create a convincing walk cycle. The shoulder movements are offset by pi, so the arms swing naturally. I've set render settings for Eevee, including sampling and resolution. Now, I will start the animation rendering!\n\n\n**Adjusting Rendering Strategy**\n\nI'm now changing to rendering a sequence of PNGs due to potential issues with the direct MP4 export using FFMPEG, which I've seen before. The render settings are changed to save individual frames in a dedicated directory, to guarantee that it doesn't crash! I'm hoping to get this right. I must not lose this work!\n\n\n**Perfecting Coordinate Handling**\n\nI'm now focusing on ensuring correct placement and parenting in my Blender Python script. The goal is to build the 3D stickman's rig with absolute precision. I've updated my `create_joint` and `create_limb` functions to correctly handle the `.parent` and `.location` assignments, so that new objects in the scene match their intended world coordinates, even after parenting, by explicitly correcting `.matrix_parent_inverse`. This also takes care of preserving transforms.\n\n\n**Refining the parenting**\n\nI am now refining my Blender Python script with improved parenting! I was missing a key point in setting locations. With local coordinates, parenting now works seamlessly, using local offsets to make the rig setup easy. It's a much cleaner method for creating the body, joint, and limb hierarchy. This setup is a much simpler approach for local positions, and this is now an example:\n*   Body: world `(0,0,4)`\n*   Neck (joint): local to Body `(0, 0, 1.2)`\n*   Head (mesh): local to Neck `(0, 0, 0.7)`\n*   Hip\\_L (joint): local to Body `(0.4, 0, -1)`\n*   Thigh\\_L (mesh): local to Hip\\_L `(0, 0, -0.6)`\n*   Knee\\_L (joint): local to Hip\\_L `(0, 0, -1.2)`\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import bpy\nimport math\nimport os\n\n# 1. Clear Scene\nbpy.ops.wm.read_factory_settings(use_empty=True)\n\n# 2. Materials\nmat_white = bpy.data.materials.new(\"White\")\nif hasattr(mat_white, 'use_nodes'):\n    mat_white.use_nodes = True\nmat_white.node_tree.nodes[\"Principled BSDF\"].inputs[\"Base Color\"].default_value = (1, 1, 1, 1)\n\nmat_black = bpy.data.materials.new(\"Black\")\nif hasattr(mat_black, 'use_nodes'):\n    mat_black.use_nodes = True\nmat_black.node_tree.nodes[\"Principled BSDF\"].inputs[\"Base Color\"].default_value = (0.01, 0.01, 0.01, 1)\n\n# Helper functions using LOCAL coordinates\ndef create_joint(name, parent, local_loc):\n    bpy.ops.object.empty_add(type='SPHERE', radius=0.2)\n    obj = bpy.context.active_object\n    obj.name = name\n    if parent:\n        obj.parent = parent\n    obj.location = local_loc\n    return obj\n\ndef create_limb(name, radius, depth, parent, local_loc):\n    bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_cylinder_add(radius=radius, depth=depth)\n    obj = bpy.context.active_object\n    obj.name = name\n    obj.parent = parent\n    obj.location = local_loc\n    obj.data.materials.append(mat_white)\n    return obj\n\n# 3. Build Rig Hierarchy\nbody = create_joint(\"Body\", None, (0, 0, 4))\n\nbpy.ops.mesh.primitive_cylinder_add(radius=0.6, depth=2.4)\ntorso = bpy.context.active_object\ntorso.parent = body\ntorso.location = (0, 0, 0)\ntorso.data.materials.append(mat_white)\n\nneck = create_joint(\"Neck\", body, (0, 0, 1.4))\nbpy.ops.mesh.primitive_uv_sphere_add(radius=0.8)\nhead = bpy.context.active_object\nhead.parent = neck\nhead.location = (0, 0, 0.8)\nhead.data.materials.append(mat_white)\n\n# Legs\nhip_L = create_joint(\"Hip_L\", body, (0.4, 0, -1.2))\nthigh_L = create_limb(\"Thigh_L\", 0.15, 1.2, hip_L, (0, 0, -0.6))\nknee_L = create_joint(\"Knee_L\", hip_L, (0, 0, -1.2))\ncalf_L = create_limb(\"Calf_L\", 0.15, 1.2, knee_L, (0, 0, -0.6))\n\nhip_R = create_joint(\"Hip_R\", body, (-0.4, 0, -1.2))\nthigh_R = create_limb(\"Thigh_R\", 0.15, 1.2, hip_R, (0, 0, -0.6))\nknee_R = create_joint(\"Knee_R\", hip_R, (0, 0, -1.2))\ncalf_R = create_limb(\"Calf_R\", 0.15, 1.2, knee_R, (0, 0, -0.6))\n\n# Arms\nshoulder_L = create_joint(\"Shoulder_L\", body, (0.8, 0, 0.8))\narm_L = create_limb(\"Arm_L\", 0.12, 1.0, shoulder_L, (0, 0, -0.5))\nelbow_L = create_joint(\"Elbow_L\", shoulder_L, (0, 0, -1.0))\nforearm_L = create_limb(\"Forearm_L\", 0.12, 1.0, elbow_L, (0, 0, -0.5))\n\nshoulder_R = create_joint(\"Shoulder_R\", body, (-0.8, 0, 0.8))\narm_R = create_limb(\"Arm_R\", 0.12, 1.0, shoulder_R, (0, 0, -0.5))\nelbow_R = create_joint(\"Elbow_R\", shoulder_R, (0, 0, -1.0))\nforearm_R = create_limb(\"Forearm_R\", 0.12, 1.0, elbow_R, (0, 0, -0.5))\n\n# Floor\nbpy.ops.mesh.primitive_plane_add(size=30, location=(0,0,0))\nground = bpy.context.active_object\nground.data.materials.append(mat_black)\n\n# Camera & Light\nbpy.ops.object.camera_add(location=(10, -10, 5))\ncam = bpy.context.active_object\ncam.rotation_euler = (math.radians(75), 0, math.radians(45))\nbpy.context.scene.camera = cam\n\nbpy.ops.object.light_add(type='SUN', location=(5,-5,5))\nlight = bpy.context.active_object\nlight.data.energy = 3.0\n\n# 4. Animate (150 frames = 5s @ 30fps)\nfps = 30\nbpy.context.scene.render.fps = fps\nbpy.context.scene.frame_start = 1\nbpy.context.scene.frame_end = 150\n\nfor f in range(1, 151):\n    t = f / fps\n    wp = t * 6 # Walk speed\n    \n    # Body bob\n    body.location[2] = 4 + 0.2 * abs(math.sin(wp))\n    body.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"location\", frame=f)\n    \n    # Walk Kinematics\n    hip_L.rotation_euler[0] = math.sin(wp) * 0.7\n    hip_L.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    hip_R.rotation_euler[0] = math.sin(wp + math.pi) * 0.7\n    hip_R.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    knee_L.rotation_euler[0] = max(0, math.sin(wp)) * 0.8\n    knee_L.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    knee_R.rotation_euler[0] = max(0, math.sin(wp + math.pi)) * 0.8\n    knee_R.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    shoulder_L.rotation_euler[0] = math.sin(wp + math.pi) * 0.5\n    shoulder_L.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    shoulder_R.rotation_euler[0] = math.sin(wp) * 0.5\n    shoulder_R.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    elbow_L.rotation_euler[0] = -max(0, math.sin(wp + math.pi)) * 0.5\n    elbow_L.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n    \n    elbow_R.rotation_euler[0] = -max(0, math.sin(wp)) * 0.5\n    elbow_R.keyframe_insert(data_path=\"rotation_euler\", frame=f)\n\n    # Move body forward slightly to fake a treadmill passing under\n    # Or just let him walk in place, which looks fine for a walk cycle loop.\n\n# 5. Render Settings\nscene = bpy.context.scene\ntry:\n    scene.render.engine = 'BLENDER_EEVEE_NEXT'\nexcept:\n    scene.render.engine = 'BLENDER_EEVEE'\n\nscene.eevee.taa_render_samples = 16\nscene.render.resolution_x = 854\nscene.render.resolution_y = 480\n\noutput_dir = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\manim-projects\\3d_stickman_frames\\\\\"\nif not os.path.exists(output_dir):\n    os.makedirs(output_dir)\n\nscene.render.filepath = output_dir\nscene.render.image_settings.file_format = 'PNG'\n\n# Render\nbpy.ops.render.render(animation=True)\n","Description":"Blender script to create a 3D rigged walking stickman.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\manim-projects\\3d_stickman.py","toolAction":"Writing 3D Stickman Blender script","toolSummary":"Write 3D Stickman Script"}}]}
